I want to start today with a correction  if I get something wrong or if I'm not  clear or if I'm incomplete about  something I always try to do these at  the top of the show I have no intention  of hiding the corrections on the back  page so to speak as is often the case  with newspapers or other Publications  um so let me get right into that  yesterday I did this segment about Fox  News propagandist Tucker Carlson siding  with Vladimir Putin and sort of writing  off Ukraine saying Ukraine isn't even a  democracy and sort of softly justifying  or defending or excusing Vladimir  Putin's invasion of Ukraine and I made a  lot of critiques of Ukraine in that  segment that are true including that  there are concerns in Ukraine about  women's rights there is corruption in  Ukraine there's a lack of true rule of  law in Ukraine number of other  concerning elements in Ukraine but I  didn't make clear that Tucker is wrong  about Ukraine not being a democracy  Ukraine is a democracy more or less and  certainly way more than Russia is if you  look at the freedom index  freedomhouse.org you'll see that Ukraine  is a 60 out of a hundred on the freedom  index which is sort of a measure of  democracy uh Russia is a 20. so 60 puts  Ukraine as partly free 20 puts Russia as  not free so if I didn't make clear or I  misstated Ukraine is a democracy albeit  a flawed one and Ukraine is moving in  the direction of being more democratic  whereas recently Russia has moved in the  direction of being less Democratic  um the Ukrainian president zielinski  genuinely won an election a real  election he's in over his head for sure  there were some problems with the  election but it was he won he he won uh  he did not control the election in the  way that Vladimir Putin controls  elections in Russia  um and so this is a correction I didn't  make that clear yesterday zielinski is  not an authoritarian autocrat Vladimir  Putin is and that is a crucial  difference between Russia and Ukraine it  doesn't resolve any other issue it  doesn't excuse the things that are not  okay in Ukraine uh but I appreciate the  opportunity to make that correction
 

